 LoadTatinAndRunTests;debugFlag
⍝ This function is called when the test suite needs to be executed in batch mode.
⍝ Honors -debug from the command line if specified.
 #.⎕EX'Tatin'
 {}({⍵.fastLoad←1 ⋄ ⍵}⎕NS'')⎕SE.Link.Import'#.Tatin' './APLSource'
 :If 0=#.Tatin.⎕NC'CiderConfig'
⍝ Only Cider creates `CiderConfig`, and a plain Link import does not, but the test suite needs
⍝ `CiderConfig.HOME`: without it `TestCases.∆CopyTestServerDataTo` fails with a VALUE ERROR
⍝ before the first test case. A batch run starts in the project folder, so that is HOME.
     #.Tatin.CiderConfig←⎕NS''
     #.Tatin.CiderConfig.HOME←¯1↓⊃1 ⎕NPARTS''
     ⍞←'CiderConfig.HOME set to ',#.Tatin.CiderConfig.HOME,⎕UCS 10
 :EndIf
 debugFlag←'-debug'≡'-debug '{0=+/b←⍺∘≡¨(≢⍺)↑¨' ',⍨¨⎕C¨⍵:'' ⋄ (b⍳1)⊃⍵}⊣2 ⎕NQ #'GetCommandLineArgs'
 debugFlag #.Tatin.TestCases.RunBatchTests 1
⍝Done
